note: a number can be written with an exponent: digits, e or E, an optional sign, digits
print(1e3, 1E3, 1.5e-3, 2e+2, 12e0, 0e5)
print(1e3 is 1000, 2.5e-1 + 0.75, -1e2, 1e2 ** 2, 5e-1 * 4)

note: what is printed in exponent form can be written back
print(1e15, 1e21, 6.02e23, 1e-7, 1.7976931348623157e308)
number avogadro = 6.02214076e23
print(avogadro / 1e23)

note: it is a number wherever a number can stand
list items = [10, 20, 30]
print(items[2e0], items[1e0 ~ 2])
loop repeat number i = 1 ~ 3e0 do:
    print(i)
end
print(1e3.to_str() + "!", 1e2 > 99)

note: a number so small that it cannot be told from zero is zero
print(1e-400)

note: an `e` that no digits follow is not an exponent: this is the number 1 and the word end
if true do: print(1) end
number e5 = 7
print(2 + e5)

note: to_number reads the same form
use DLC:convert
print(to_number("1e3") is 1e3, to_number("2.5E-1"))
